From: zhaosiying12138 <neucszhaopeng2016@163.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:18:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 38/42] gpu-compute: complete wavefront counter accounting and
 dispatch bookkeeping

Extends the counter family already repaired at HEAD, where per-instruction
bookkeeping was gated on static instruction flags that a valid instruction
legitimately lacks, so the reservation made at issue was never released and the
wave stalled forever on a later s_waitcnt.

The same shape recurs for expcnt: an export or GDS instruction that never
reached the path which decrements it left the wave's expcnt permanently
non-zero, and the next s_waitcnt expcnt(0) blocked. Wavefront gains explicit
accounting for the three outstanding counters, and the dispatcher and dynamic
instruction carry the state that makes a leak visible rather than silent.

UNVERIFIED AT HANDOFF: carried forward from an earlier session and compiled
into the running binary, but not accepted by a completed model run.

